# 2026-07-31: CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC tried (confirmed via env/nowhere.c
# that the previous CONFIG_ENV_IS_NOWHERE=y backend never actually
# persisted saveenv/env_save() anywhere -- silently broke the
# bootcount/bootlimit boot-supervision fallback) but REVERTED same day:
# hardware-tested and found it hangs the board completely, before even
# "DRAM:"/"NAND:"/"MMC:" print -- confirmed via a clean .config diff
# against a known-good week-old .config.old that CONFIG_ENV_IS_IN_MMC
# was the ONLY functional difference. Root cause not yet found (see
# docs/DEVICE_TEST_CHECKLIST_2026-07-18.md §83) -- reverted to restore
# basic bootability rather than keep guessing on live hardware. The
# bootcount persistence problem (see §82) is open again until this is
# revisited properly. Do NOT re-enable without understanding why this
# hangs so early first.
